  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0192 database is designed to manage a bookstore's inventory and customer information. The database contains 21 tables that work together to store data about authors, books, publishers, customers, orders, and more. The author table holds information about the writers behind the books, including their name, a brief summary, and a picture. The book table stores details about each book, such as its product ID, name, description, price, and ISBN number. The publisher table contains information about the companies that publish the books, including their name, address, email, and phone number. The storeuser table holds customer data, including their username, first and last name, email, address, and login history. The role table defines the different roles within the bookstore, such as administrator or customer. The warehouse table stores information about the physical storage locations, including their name, address, phone number, and square footage. The storeorder table tracks customer orders, including the order number, status, billing and shipping information, and the time the order was placed. The cart table stores the items currently in a customer's shopping cart, while the cart_coupon and cart_product tables link customers to coupons and products they have added to their cart. The order_coupon and order_product tables store the coupons and products that have been applied to a customer's order. The publishes table links books to their publishers, while the stored_in table tracks the stock levels of each product in each warehouse. The user_role table assigns roles to customers, and the writes table links authors to the books they have written.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context:\n\nThe project involves developing an online bookstore that offers a wide selection of books and related accessories. This platform aims to provide an engaging and user-friendly experience for both customers wanting to purchase books and business stakeholders managing the store's operations. \n\n2) Objectives:\n\n- Facilitate the purchase and sale of books online.\n- Allow users to manage their shopping experience and orders seamlessly.\n- Enable store owners to maintain and manage inventory efficiently.\n- Provide publishers with tools to manage their stock and receive commissions.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users:\n\n- Customers: Individuals who wish to browse, purchase, and track books.\n- Owners: Individuals responsible for inventory management, sales tracking, and platform administration.\n- Publishers: Partners who publish books, manage stock, and receive commissions.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions:\n\n- User Features:\n  - Search for available books in the inventory.\n  - Add selected books to a virtual shopping cart.\n  - Sign in to a personal account for a personalized experience.\n  - Place orders for books in the cart.\n  - Track the status of placed orders.\n\n- Owner Features:\n  - Add, edit, or remove book listings.\n  - Manage publisher information and their book offerings.\n  - Monitor sales performance and key performance indicators (KPIs).\n\n- Publisher Features:\n  - Receive commissions for sold books authored by them.\n  - Receive notifications when book stock falls below a specified threshold.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions:\n\n- The system should ensure a secure and user-friendly interface.\n- Perform efficiently to handle numerous transactions and updates concurrently.\n- Secure payment processing with industry-standard encryption.\n- Scalable architecture to support growth in users and inventory.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0192.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0192\nCREATE TABLE `author` (\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `summary` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `picture` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`author_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `isbn` varchar(13) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `publisher` (\n  `publisher_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`publisher_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `storeuser` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `login_history` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `role` (\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `role_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`role_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `warehouse` (\n  `warehouse_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `square_footage` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`warehouse_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `storeorder` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `billing_info` text NOT NULL,\n  `shipping_info` text NOT NULL,\n  `order_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `cart` (\n  `cart_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`cart_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `cart_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `storeuser` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `cart_coupon` (\n  `cart_coupon_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cart_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `coupon_code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`cart_coupon_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `cart_coupon_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cart_id`) REFERENCES `cart` (`cart_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `cart_product` (\n  `cart_product_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cart_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`cart_product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `cart_product_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cart_id`) REFERENCES `cart` (`cart_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `cart_product_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order_coupon` (\n  `order_coupon_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `coupon_code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_coupon_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_coupon_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `storeorder` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order_product` (\n  `order_product_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_product_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `storeorder` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_product_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `publishes` (\n  `publish_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `publisher_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`publish_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `publishes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `publishes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`publisher_id`) REFERENCES `publisher` (`publisher_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `stored_in` (\n  `stored_in_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `warehouse_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `stock_level` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`stored_in_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `stored_in_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `stored_in_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`warehouse_id`) REFERENCES `warehouse` (`warehouse_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_role` (\n  `user_role_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_role_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_role_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `storeuser` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_role_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `role` (`role_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `writes` (\n  `writes_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`writes_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `writes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`author_id`) REFERENCES `author` (`author_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `writes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
